<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.3" snapToGrid="false">
  <code>breed [citizens citizen]
breed [police officer]

globals [agent-vision]

citizens-own [hardship grievance risk-aversion perceived-arrest-risk active?]
turtles-own [moved-this-tick?]

to setup
  clear-all
  set agent-vision vision_in_patches

  let citizen-count round (0.7 * count patches)
  ask n-of citizen-count patches [
    sprout-citizens 1 [
      set hardship random-float 1
      set risk-aversion random-float 1
      set grievance hardship * (1 - legitimacy)
      set active? false
      set color blue
    ]
  ]
  let police-count round (0.04 * count patches)
  ask n-of police-count patches with [not any? turtles-here] [
    sprout-police 1 
  ]
  update-all-agents
  update-police-colors
  reset-ticks
end

to go
  if not any? turtles [ stop ]
  ask turtles [
    move-randomly
    if breed = citizens [ update-citizen-state ]
  ]
  tick
end

to update-citizen-state  ; citizen procedure
  set grievance hardship * (1 - legitimacy)
  set perceived-arrest-risk ifelse-value (any? police in-radius agent-vision)
    [risk-when-police-visible]
    [0]
  set active? (grievance - risk-aversion * perceived-arrest-risk) &gt; activation-threshold
  set color ifelse-value active? [red] [blue]
end

to move-randomly
  let destinations (patches in-radius agent-vision) with [not any? turtles-here]
  set moved-this-tick? any? destinations
  if moved-this-tick? [ move-to one-of destinations ]
end



to update-all-agents
  ask turtles [
    set moved-this-tick? false
  ]
  
end

to update-police-colors
  ask police [set color yellow]
  
end


to-report percent-active
  if not any? citizens [ report 0 ]
  report 100 * count citizens with [active?] / count citizens
end</code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="220" wrappingAllowedX="true" y="10" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="0" height="404" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="10.0" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="true" width="404" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="39" updateMode="1" maxPxcor="39" minPxcor="0"></view>
    <button x="15" y="20" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="95" display="Setup">setup</button>
    <button x="15" y="72" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="95" display="Go">go</button>
    <input x="13" multiline="false" y="129" height="60" variable="vision_in_patches" type="number" width="192">2.0</input>
    <input x="13" y="203" height="60" width="192" variable="legitimacy" type="number" multiline="false">0.82</input>
    <input x="13" y="273" height="60" width="192" variable="activation-threshold" type="number" multiline="false">0.1</input>
    <monitor x="220" y="430" height="61" width="150" precision="1" fontSize="11" display="% active">percent-active</monitor>
    <input x="13" y="343" height="60" width="192" variable="risk-when-police-visible" type="number" multiline="false">0.1</input>
    <plot x="220" y="504" width="404" height="200" display="% active over time" xAxis="Tick" yAxis="% active" xMin="0.0" xMax="25.0" yMin="0.0" yMax="100.0" autoPlotX="true" autoPlotY="false" legend="false">
      <setup></setup>
      <update></update>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Active" color="-2674135" legend="false">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>if ticks &gt; 0 [ plotxy ticks percent-active ]</update>
      </pen>
    </plot>
  </widgets>
  <info>## O_m2 · Local deterrence

Enter **legitimacy**, **activation-threshold**, and **risk-when-police-visible** as values from 0 to 1. At Setup citizens draw fixed hardship and risk aversion. Each citizen stores grievance as hardship × (1 − legitimacy).

Citizens start blue. Each turn a citizen moves if possible, updates grievance, and checks for officers within the same radius used for movement. Perceived arrest risk is zero when no officer is visible and equals **risk-when-police-visible** otherwise. The citizen turns red when grievance minus risk aversion × perceived arrest risk exceeds the activation threshold. Police continue to move to vacant patches.

Keep inputs fixed during Go. The **% active over time** plot starts at tick 1. Moving officers and citizens can change perceived risk and activation even while grievance stays fixed.

## Citizen decision rule

After the movement step, Go calls `update-citizen-state` for each citizen. In O_m2, the activation line is:

```netlogo
set active? (grievance - risk-aversion * perceived-arrest-risk) &gt; activation-threshold
```

O_m1 uses the same procedure name and compares grievance directly with the threshold. In O_m2, when no officer is in view, perceived arrest risk is zero and the rules give the same decision.</info>
